{"run_id": "b717dc7169cf4570a0bfd13dceeb0c86", "study": "output_length_natural_pilot", "model_key": "gpt_oss_20b", "model_name": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_condition": "role_rubric", "decoding": "soft", "thinking": true, "seed": 42, "claim_id": 31, "claim": "A honey badger would fit inside an oven.", "stance": "support", "argument_id": "rank_1", "argument": "Adult honey badgers stand roughly 25–30 cm at the shoulder and can curl their 60–77 cm bodies, while a typical household oven cavity is about 60 cm wide, 45 cm deep, and 40 cm high, so the animal could physically fit when curled.", "reference_rank": 1, "raw_output": "analysisWe need to evaluate the argument: \"Adult honey badgers stand roughly 25–30 cm at the shoulder and can curl their 60–77 cm bodies, while a typical household oven cavity is about 60 cm wide, 45 cm deep, and 40 cm high, so the animal could physically fit when curled.\"\n\nWe need to assess factuality, relevance, logical quality, effectiveness. Provide a single integer score 0-100.\n\nLet's analyze:\n\nFactuality: Are the facts accurate? Adult honey badger shoulder height 25-30 cm? Let's check: Honey badger (Mellivora capensis) adult body length 70-90 cm, shoulder height 30-35 cm? Actually typical adult size: length 70-90 cm, shoulder height about 30-35 cm. So 25-30 cm is somewhat low but plausible. Body length 60-77 cm? Might be 70-90 cm. So body length range 60-77 cm is slightly low but could be for smaller individuals. So facts are roughly correct but not precise. Might be okay.\n\nOven cavity dimensions: typical household oven cavity: about 60 cm wide, 45 cm deep, 40 cm high. That seems plausible. So facts credible.\n\nRelevance: The claim is \"A honey badger would fit inside an oven.\" The argument provides physical measurements to support that it would fit. So relevant.\n\nLogical quality: The reasoning: if the honey badger can curl to 60-77 cm length, and oven cavity 60 cm wide, 45 cm deep, 40 cm high, then it could physically fit. Ne